# Experiment sandboxes and archived run evidence, together tens of MB of model transcripts and
# scored results, some of which embed rows returned by the datasets. Re-running the command in the
# docs writes new files here, but it does not reproduce what is already in them: observer records
# and eval/runs are read back as the denominator for findings.py's cumulative per-probe rates and for
# trend.py's run-over-run comparison, so deleting them moves those numbers rather than tidying
# anything. Treat "regenerated" as "this path will be repopulated", never as "this is disposable".
#
# These are globs rather than one name each: listing them individually meant a newly named sandbox
# was committed by default and 82MB of transcripts ended up in the history of a repo that had no
# ignore rule covering them.
eval/arms*/
eval/attrib*/
eval/attrib-suite*/
eval/combination/floor-recheck/
eval/combination/run-*/
eval/harness*/
eval/noise*/
eval/observer/.agent-session
eval/observer/.tick.lock
eval/observer/findings.json
eval/observer/records/
eval/runs/
eval/validate*/

# Operator-supplied input, and long-run transcripts. grok/ is a brief and question suite that is
# theirs rather than ours, so it never enters a commit. logs/ holds tmux and tick output.
grok/
logs/

# Python build and cache artifacts. pytest writes its own .gitignore containing `*` inside
# .pytest_cache/, so that one does not need listing here. These are recreated by running Python or
# pytest rather than by any command in the docs, which is why they are listed apart from the
# sandboxes above.
.coverage
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Local secrets.
.env

# Coverage HTML.
htmlcov/
